\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{Pair-level statistics for the rows of Table~3 of the main paper (exp\_0058, saved outputs only). $n$: pairs; range and mean: per-pair values (Recovery, found-rate or witness share, or a difference); CI: 95\% $t$-interval on the pair means (-- for $n<4$). Exact $p$: ``sign'' is the one-sided exact sign test ($k$ of $n$ pairs on the claimed side); ``flip'' is the exact sign-flip permutation test on the pair means (one-sided for $>0$ claims, two-sided for the $\pm 0.10$ band rows, where $k/n$ counts pairs inside the band); ``perm.'' is the Monte Carlo permutation test of the Spearman correlation. Min.\ $p$: smallest value the test can attain with $n$ pairs. MixedLM: intercept (SE) and one-sided Wald $p$ against the row's threshold ($0.9$ for CF-diff, $0.2$ for Grad-diff); for the rotation row, the slope on $\hat  \alpha $ (SE) and its two-sided $p$. The MixedLM is a sensitivity check only: with little variance between pairs it treats points as independent, so its $p$ values (down to $10^{-66}$) are far smaller than the pair-level ones and are not evidence at the pair level. Three registered readouts in Table~3 are counts of pairs only: witness $\ge $ margin score $+0.2$ (7 of 8) and, for ResNet-8 on split D, Grad-diff $<0.2$ on offsets and rotation above offset (0 of 3 each).}}{4}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:s1}{{1}{4}{Pair-level statistics for the rows of Table~3 of the main paper (exp\_0058, saved outputs only). $n$: pairs; range and mean: per-pair values (Recovery, found-rate or witness share, or a difference); CI: 95\% $t$-interval on the pair means (-- for $n<4$). Exact $p$: ``sign'' is the one-sided exact sign test ($k$ of $n$ pairs on the claimed side); ``flip'' is the exact sign-flip permutation test on the pair means (one-sided for $>0$ claims, two-sided for the $\pm 0.10$ band rows, where $k/n$ counts pairs inside the band); ``perm.'' is the Monte Carlo permutation test of the Spearman correlation. Min.\ $p$: smallest value the test can attain with $n$ pairs. MixedLM: intercept (SE) and one-sided Wald $p$ against the row's threshold ($0.9$ for CF-diff, $0.2$ for Grad-diff); for the rotation row, the slope on $\hat \alpha $ (SE) and its two-sided $p$. The MixedLM is a sensitivity check only: with little variance between pairs it treats points as independent, so its $p$ values (down to $10^{-66}$) are far smaller than the pair-level ones and are not evidence at the pair level. Three registered readouts in Table~3 are counts of pairs only: witness $\ge $ margin score $+0.2$ (7 of 8) and, for ResNet-8 on split D, Grad-diff $<0.2$ on offsets and rotation above offset (0 of 3 each)}{table.1}{}}
